  "description": "I/O library for the PB1151 course microcontroller kit: control LEDs and a servo, read pushbuttons, and read a TMP102 temperature sensor and an ADXL345 accelerometer over a JSON serial protocol, via USB serial or Bluetooth LE (Nordic UART Service).",
  "id": "Usn.Pb1151.DeviceKit",
  "isPrerelease": false,
  "lastEdited": "2026-08-05T11:22:42.05Z",
  "licenseExpression": "MIT",
  "licenseUrl": "https://licenses.nuget.org/MIT",
  "listed": true,
  "packageHash": "+KNQ3tndAvojS17OBoVHH8FIpLY1e4S6Un1Cic1YIBYOGkJdl5PK+fvG8n4G36AbPU9wPclDvWQzEPHove2rGQ==",
  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 55012,
  "published": "2026-08-05T11:17:25.053Z",
  "readmeFile": "README.md",
  "releaseNotes": "1.1.0: Multi-targeted the package for net10.0-windows and net10.0-windows10.0.17763.0, so it now restores in projects created from the standard WinForms/WPF templates (which target plain net10.0-windows) without editing the consuming project's TargetFramework. On net10.0-windows, everything is available except BleNusEx (BLE requires the WinRT projections only available on the versioned windows10.0.17763.0 TFM); bump the consuming project's TargetFramework to net10.0-windows10.0.17763.0 to use BLE. 1.0.1: Lowered the minimum target Windows version from 10.0.19041.0 to 10.0.17763.0 (Windows 10, version 1809) to relax consuming-project TargetFramework requirements; no API changes. 1.0.0: Initial release. JsonSerialController with LedControl, ServoControl, ButtonControl, and SensorControl (TMP102 temperature, ADXL345 acceleration). Two transports: SerialPortEx (USB serial) and BleNusEx (BLE Nordic UART Service), both behind ISerialDataReadWrite.",
